+## Prospective component ordinary-image activation amendment
+
+This addition requires exact separate human installation. It creates no execution
+permission. Historical component decisions, /2 consumers, selections and receipts
+retain their original subjects; K2 authority cannot authorize a component identity.
+
+The component /3 production route shall use the accepted digest-pinned native image
+and ordinary debug/release executables with one admitted saved stdin stream and EOF.
+Private cfg(test) witnesses shall not supply ordinary-process entry counts. Consume
+success through structural validation, the matching /3 checker and independently
+frozen literals/input/full-engine anchors. Retain bounded attempts and complete
+framing, streams, status, slot, resource and exact-created-ID cleanup evidence before
+interpretation. Reopen and independently consume all six bound initial receipts
+before replay; preserve failed attempts and the historical 124/1368 schedule.
+The 120/1344 proposal remains unapproved. Public acceptance requires a separately
+reviewed ordinary-EOF campaign contract and implementation, not private acceptance/1.
+
+The Python bootstrap (including typing's compatibility pseudo-modules), interpreter,
+stdlib/cache candidates, extensions, loader/DSOs and configuration require external
+immutable bindings. An externally supplied manifest digest is not self-authorizing;
+private read-only copies and a benign import launch do not establish immutable
+placement, exhaustive loaded-code assurance or A-F3 closure. The stopped real-D11
+startup-substitution/defense-revert activity remains deferred and must not be retried,
+transferred or replaced with an ordinary positive claim. Required unavailable evidence
+continues to block public first use unless separately resolved by the original reviewer
+and exact human decisions; this amendment supplies no waiver.
+
+D3 inventory/2, record/2, selector/2 and exact envelope/provenance laws remain separate.
+The prospective v6 adapter uses the same ordinary EOF transport but leaves entry/site
+observations unobserved. An expected zero-entry value, exact message, null pointer or
+source hash does not establish universal guard reach. D3 installation, review and
+execution permission require their own exact subject and decision.
+
+Before activation source freeze, reconcile A/B adapter, consumer, preparation,
+validation-test, startup and any installed proposal postimages. Then bind actual
+BuildInputs, generated identity, accepted tools/lock/cache/features and a reviewed
+full-ID capture ledger/monitor. No historical binary inherits later source identities.
+Capture/build execution, root placement, immutable public environment, genuine
+selector/HostRecord/profile authority and public campaign are separate gates. Missing
+construction reads and the three historical candidate-03 gaps remain unresolved.
+The /2 same-engine/same-instant acquired-release first-use restriction applies in all
+directions, including write/write and unclassified cases; no /2 repair or waiver is
+made. Genuine human L1 workings and U0024 remain unchanged; no qualification or U4
+closure follows.
